-- app schema: the synthetic dataset, as data rather than as parquet.
--
-- Regenerate with:
--   pg_dump "$DATABASE_URL" --schema=app --no-owner --no-comments \
--       --quote-all-identifiers > etl/seed_app.sql
--   (then re-attach the role block below, which pg_dump cannot emit)
--
--   AND strip what newer tools emit that older ones reject — both broke CI:
--     * `\restrict` / `\unrestrict` lines (pg_dump 18+): meta-commands a
--       psql 16/17 client calls an invalid command, and ON_ERROR_STOP makes
--       that fatal. They guard against a MALICIOUS dump; this one is ours.
--     * `SET transaction_timeout = 0;` — the parameter exists only on
--       PostgreSQL 17+, so a 16 server errors on it.
--   sed -i -E '/^\\(restrict|unrestrict) /d; /^SET transaction_timeout = 0;$/d' etl/seed_app.sql
--     * any `ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES FOR ROLE "<you>"` line: pg_dump names the
--       role that created the ACL on YOUR machine, which exists nowhere else.
--       The unqualified version in the trailer below does the same job portably.
--   sed -i '/ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES FOR ROLE/d' etl/seed_app.sql
--
-- WHAT THIS REPLACES. `etl/load_postgres.py` builds this schema from
-- backend/data/*.parquet, driven by etl/manifest.yaml. The parquet files are no
-- longer in the repository, so this file is the dataset. manifest.yaml STAYS —
-- app/bot/schema.py and app/tools/sql_tools.py derive queryable columns, the PII
-- set and the run_sql denylist from it, and none of that comes from here.
--
-- CONTAINS: 25 reps, 938 doctors, and their visits/brands/chemists/hooks/metrics.
-- DOES NOT CONTAIN: any conversation or message. Chat history lives in `public`
-- and is created empty by etl/chat_history.sql.
--
-- THE ROLE BLOCK IS NOT OPTIONAL. `qorvexa_ro` is the boundary the whole tool
-- layer depends on (see docs/claude/security-invariants.md §1.5): the agent's SQL
-- runs as this role, and `app.reps.password_hash` is withheld by a column-level
-- grant rather than by a query filter. pg_dump emits the per-object ACLs but
-- cannot create a role, so the role is created here first — otherwise every
-- GRANT below fails and the schema loads with no read-only role at all.

\set ON_ERROR_STOP on

-- The role's password comes from RO_PASSWORD when set, so docker-compose can
-- pass one through and nothing has to be edited in this file. `\getenv` needs
-- psql 16+; the fallback matches DATABASE_URL_RO in .env.example.
\set ro_password 'qorvexa_ro'
\getenv env_ro_password RO_PASSWORD
\if :{?env_ro_password}
\set ro_password :env_ro_password
\endif

-- Deliberately NOT a DO $$ block: psql does not substitute :variables inside
-- dollar quotes, so the password would arrive literally as ":'ro_password'".
-- \gset + \if keeps the substitution outside any quoting, and :'ro_password'
-- is emitted as a properly escaped SQL literal.
SELECT NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_roles WHERE rolname = 'qorvexa_ro')
    AS create_ro_role \gset
\if :create_ro_role
CREATE ROLE "qorvexa_ro" LOGIN PASSWORD :'ro_password';
\endif

